Logic :

first store the frequency of all characters in t.
Then use a sliding window with two pointers. 
As expand the window using the right pointer,  reduce the required count of that character in the map. 
Whenever if you include a required character, increase the matched count.
Once all characters of t are matched, try to shrink the window from the left to find the minimum valid window.
Before removing a character, update the answer if the current window is smaller. 
If removing a character makes the window invalid,  stop shrinking and continue expanding again. 
This way, keep finding the smallest valid window."


Code :

class Solution {
    public String minWindow(String s, String t) {
        if(s.length()<t.length()){
            return "";
        }
        HashMap<Character,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
        int c=0;
        int left=0;
        int len=Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        int start=0;
        for(char ch:t.toCharArray()){
            map.put(ch,map.getOrDefault(ch,0)+1);
        }
        for(int right=0;right<s.length();right++){
            char ch=s.charAt(right);
            if(map.getOrDefault(ch,0)>0){
                c++;
            }
            map.put(ch,map.getOrDefault(ch,0)-1);
            while(c==t.length()){
                char ch1=s.charAt(left);
                if(len>(right-left+1)){
                    len=right-left+1;
                    start=left;
                }
                if(map.get(ch1)==0){
                    c--;
                }
                left++;
                map.put(ch1,map.get(ch1)+1);
            }
        }
        if(len==Integer.MAX_VALUE){
            return "";
        }
        return s.substring(start,start+len);
    }
}
